 ## Overview
-NeRF pre-processing stabilizes training by constraining the dynamic range of image features and normalizing camera geometry before optimization. It addresses feature fluctuations caused by varying exposure, illumination, and occlusions, which otherwise lead to unstable MLP training [S2]. Unlike sibling methods that modify architecture or loss functions, this approach treats normalization as a conventional data preparation step to ensure inputs fall within the effective range of positional encodings [S2].
